---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { meta } from "../i18n/meta";
import { SITE_URL as siteUrl } from "../lib/site";
import { breadcrumbLd } from "../lib/breadcrumbs";
import { ogImageFor } from "../lib/og";

const m = meta.en.terms;

const pageLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: m.title,
  description: m.description,
  inLanguage: "en",
  url: new URL("/terms-and-conditions", siteUrl).toString(),
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${siteUrl}/#website` },
};
---

<Layout
  title={m.title}
  description={m.description}
  ogImage={ogImageFor("/terms-and-conditions")}
  jsonLd={[
    breadcrumbLd("en", [
      { name: "Home", path: "/" },
      { name: "Terms & Conditions", path: "/terms-and-conditions" },
    ]),
    pageLd,
  ]}
>
  <main class="min-h-screen bg-canvas text-white">
    <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
      <p
        class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold tracking-[1.8px] text-mint uppercase"
      >
        Legal
      </p>
      <h1
        class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl leading-[0.9] tracking-[1.07px] sm:text-6xl"
      >
        Terms &amp; Conditions
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-secondary">Last updated: 2026</p>

      <div
        class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary"
      >
        <p>
          These Terms &amp; Conditions govern your use of World Cup Draft
          Simulator. It is a free browser football game and a fantasy football
          world cup draft simulator. They apply to the football simulator, the
          football draft simulator, the teams index and every page of the world
          cup fantasy game. By opening the app you agree to these terms. If you
          do not agree, do not use the site. We wrote them in plain language. A
          world cup simulator should be as clear about its rules as its
          gameplay.
        </p>
        <p>
          The app is a made-up, non-commercial game for fun. These terms show
          that. No accounts. No purchases. No real-money bets. If anything is
          unclear, the contact page is open. We will explain a clause in
          everyday words.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-secondary">
        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            1. Acceptance of terms
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            By using My World Cup XI (the "Site") you agree to these Terms &amp;
            Conditions. If you do not agree, do not use the Site. You agree the
            moment you open the football simulator in your browser. There is no
            account to make. No box to tick. Playing is your agreement.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            These terms cover the whole fantasy football world cup experience.
            The football draft simulator. The teams index. The how-to-play
            guide. The draft tool. They work with our Privacy Policy. That
            policy says what little data the world cup fantasy game touches. If
            a court says one part is invalid, the rest still applies. We may
            update the terms over time. The version here with its "Last updated"
            date is the one in force.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The app is a free browser football game with no download and no
            sign-up. So agreeing costs you nothing. It only asks you to use the
            interactive football simulator as described below. If you use the
            site for a school, club or community, you confirm you can bind that
            group. If you ever disagree with a change, just stop playing and
            clear your storage. There is no account to close. A world cup
            simulator built for fun should set fair, clear rules. This section
            is where that agreement begins. Whether you arrived as a football
            draft game, a free football simulation game, or the easiest online
            football game to open between matches.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            2. Use of the service
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The Site is a free, browser-based football simulator and world cup
            simulator. It is for personal, non-commercial fun. You may use it
            under these terms. You may not use it to break any law or anyone's
            rights. The football simulator is there for you to draft, simulate
            and enjoy the world cup fantasy game. Not to sell access. Not to
            resell it. Not to wrap it in another product without permission.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Do not use the football draft simulator to harass others. Do not
            scrape or overload our servers. Do not break the app on other
            devices. The app is a free browser football game with no download.
            Normal use is exactly what it is for. Open it. Draft a squad. Share
            a screenshot of your cup. We only ask that you do not take apart the
            match engine to cheat. Respect that the squads are editorial, not
            official records.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The teams index, the how-to-play guide and the draft tool are part
            of the same interactive football simulator. The same personal-use
            rule applies to all. If you run a class, a fan group or a match-day
            event and want many to use the online football game, that is
            welcome. Keep it non-commercial and lawful. A world cup simulator
            should feel open to all. These rules are light so the fantasy
            football draft stays a shared, fun space. Not a locked service. If
            you are unsure a use fits, ask on the contact page before you build
            on the football game with no download we provide.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            3. No real-money transactions
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The game has only simulated matches, drafts and tournaments. No real
            money. No prizes. No gambling of any kind. In-game results have no
            cash value. This matters because the football simulator is a made-up
            world cup fantasy game. It is not a betting product. We built it
            that way on purpose.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The football draft simulator lets you build a dream XI from old
            squads. The match engine decides a result. That result is made for
            fun. It has no money meaning. We do not take deposits. We do not run
            pools. We do not sell paid entries. The words "fantasy" and
            "simulator" are deliberate. This is a free browser football game
            with no download. The only stake is bragging rights with friends. If
            you want daily fantasy sports or any real-money contest, this is not
            it. Use a licensed operator in your area instead.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Because the interactive football simulator is non-commercial, it
            suits classes and families. A paid game does not. We may add shared,
            no-money challenges later. For example, compare cups with friends.
            They will never involve money. Any such feature will be clear before
            you use it. A world cup simulator should stay a safe, free place to
            play. This clause keeps the online football game and the fantasy
            football draft free of betting. Whether you found it as a football
            draft game, a free football simulation game, or the easiest
            interactive football simulator to open on a phone.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            4. Intellectual property
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            All content on the Site is ours or licensed to us. This includes the
            game engine, design, text and code. It is protected by law. You may
            not copy, reuse or share it without permission. The football
            simulator, the football draft simulator, the teams index and the
            how-to-play guide are original works. The match engine that powers
            the world cup simulation is our own code. You may share your own
            results. A screenshot of a trophy. A story about a Brazil 1970 run.
            But you may not take the code, the player-rating data or the visual
            design and post them as your own.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Player names, team names and tournament names belong to their
            owners. We use them for description only. "FIFA", "EA Sports" and
            "Football Manager" are trademarks. They are not linked to this app.
            They never appear in our name or web address. This matters. World
            Cup Draft Simulator is a fantasy football draft. It is an
            interactive football simulator inspired by World Cup history. It is
            not tied to any group or publisher. The old squads are content you
            put on the pitch and simulate. They are not official records. The
            ratings are game estimates tuned for balance.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you build something on the free browser football game — a blog
            post, a lesson, a community event — you may describe and link to it.
            But you may not redistribute the app or imply partnership. A world
            cup simulator can celebrate the sport's greatest teams without
            misusing anyone's property. This section is where we draw that line.
            Whether you arrived as a football draft game, a free football
            simulation game, or the easiest online football game to open between
            matches.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            5. No warranty
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The Site is provided "as is" and "as available". There are no
            warranties, stated or implied. We do not promise the Site will never
            stop, never error, or be free of harm. We do not promise the
            simulation will match real events. The football simulator is fun
            software, not a forecast. The world cup simulation it makes is made
            up. Your draft beating a higher-rated AI side is a fun result of the
            match engine. It is not a prediction of any real tournament.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We try to keep the football draft simulator stable. We try to keep
            the penalty shootout simulator fair. But we cannot promise the app
            will never glitch. This is true across the many browsers and devices
            that open a free browser football game. We also cannot promise the
            editorial player ratings match any official source. They are tuned
            for balance inside the fantasy football draft, not copied from
            records.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Where the law allows, we disclaim implied warranties. We ask that
            you use the interactive football simulator for fun, not for
            reliance. If a bug hits your saved cup, the quick fix is usually to
            clear storage and start a new draft. Your data is local, so the
            reset is clean. None of this cuts any consumer rights you have under
            local law. Those always apply. A world cup simulator should be
            honest that it is a game. This clause says plainly that the online
            football game and the football game with no download are offered
            without guarantees. Whether you found us as a football draft game, a
            free football simulation game, or simply the easiest interactive
            football simulator to open on a phone.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            6. Limitation of liability
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any
            damages from your use of the Site. The football simulator is free.
            It has no account. It stores your drafts on your device. So the most
            you can lose from a fault is the time on one cup. And that is rare.
            The world cup fantasy game is built to be light and tough.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We are not liable for indirect or follow-on losses. For example, if
            a simulated result hurts your office pool. Or if the football draft
            simulator is down when you want to play. We are also not responsible
            for how you read the editorial squads or the player-rating data.
            They are game estimates, not official stats. Nothing here limits
            liability the law says we cannot exclude. This clause does not touch
            rights the law gives you.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The app is a free browser football game with no download. So the
            real risk to you is tiny. We kept this section short for that
            reason. If a problem occurs, the best step is the contact page. We
            will look into it. The interactive football simulator improves most
            from real reports, not formal claims. A world cup simulator should
            be a low-stakes place to play. This limit keeps the fantasy football
            draft and the online football game that way. Whether you arrived as
            a football draft game, a free football simulation game, or the
            easiest interactive football simulator to open between matches.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            7. Changes
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may change these terms at any time. If you keep using the Site
            after a change, you accept the new terms. When we update, we refresh
            the "Last updated" date at the top. So you can see which version is
            in force. If a change is big — for example, if the football
            simulator added a feature that changed the personal, non-commercial
            nature of the world cup fantasy game — we say so clearly. Where the
            law requires, we ask before it starts. Small changes may happen
            without notice. A wording fix. Or a new football formation in the
            draft tool.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We suggest you check back now and then. This is true if you use the
            teams index or the how-to-play guide as a reference. The spirit will
            not change. The free browser football game stays free. Stays
            non-commercial. Keeps your drafts on your device. If you disagree
            with an update, just stop playing and clear your storage. No account
            to close. No download to uninstall.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The interactive football simulator should keep its promises as it
            grows. Whether we add more old squads, a deeper penalty shootout
            simulator, or richer sharing. A world cup simulator built on trust
            changes its rules openly. This section is where we commit to that.
            Whether you found us as a football draft game, a free football
            simulation game, or simply the easiest online football game to open
            between matches.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="font-display text-xl tracking-[0.5px] text-white">
            8. Contact
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Questions about these terms? Or about how the football simulator
            should be used? We can explain any clause in plain words. The
            fastest way is the contact page. Write to us about anything. A
            wording question. Or a feature idea for the football draft
            simulator. The world cup fantasy game has no account. So there is
            nothing to "cancel" if you disagree with a change. You just stop
            playing and clear your storage.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We also welcome notes from parents, teachers and group leaders. They
            use the free browser football game in class or on match day. They
            want to know the rules. You can reach us whether you found the app
            as a football draft game, a free football simulation game or an
            interactive football simulator. We read every message, even during a
            real tournament. Terms are not a wall between us and the players.
            They are the shared deal that keeps the online football game fair
            and free.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If something here is unclear, tell us in everyday language. We will
            answer in the same. <a class="text-mint underline" href="/contact/"
              >Contact us</a
            > and help keep the fantasy football draft as open as it is fun.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main></Layout
>
